WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.507
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.507 --> 00:00:03.123
My name is Lily Ma

00:00:03.123 --> 00:00:05.099
and my one word is extraordinary.

00:00:05.099 --> 00:00:06.737
I believe that every human being

00:00:06.737 --> 00:00:09.575
is capable of doing extraordinary things.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.166
So to help you on your journey

00:00:11.166 --> 00:00:14.209
today's message is follow your heart.

00:00:14.209 --> 00:00:16.725
Over to you, Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson.

00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:18.721
(rooster crowing)

00:00:18.721 --> 00:00:21.274
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:21.274 --> 00:00:24.250
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:28.466
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:28.466 --> 00:00:30.776
- I found that with depression,

00:00:30.776 --> 00:00:32.699
one of the most important
things you could realize

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.289
is that you're not alone.

00:00:34.289 --> 00:00:35.606
You're not the first to go through it

00:00:35.606 --> 00:00:37.154
and you're not going to be
the last to go through it

00:00:37.154 --> 00:00:39.203
and oftentimes it happens.

00:00:39.203 --> 00:00:41.219
You just, you feel like you're alone

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:43.217
and you feel like it's only you

00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:45.632
and you're in your bubble

00:00:45.632 --> 00:00:48.715
and I wish I had someone at that time

00:00:53.231 --> 00:00:54.576
who could just pull me aside,

00:00:54.576 --> 00:00:56.425
"Hey, it's going to be okay.

00:00:56.425 --> 00:00:57.482
"It's going to be okay."

00:00:57.482 --> 00:00:58.718
So I wish I knew that.

00:00:58.718 --> 00:01:01.162
We just got to remember,

00:01:01.162 --> 00:01:05.575
hold on to that fundamental
quality of faith.

00:01:05.575 --> 00:01:06.408
Have faith

00:01:07.751 --> 00:01:10.584
and on the other side of your pain

00:01:11.421 --> 00:01:12.921
is something good.

00:01:13.933 --> 00:01:16.433
After about a month and a half

00:01:17.856 --> 00:01:20.707
of staying in that little
apartment and cleaning,

00:01:20.707 --> 00:01:22.796
I got a phone call from the head coach

00:01:22.796 --> 00:01:24.162
of the team who cut me.

00:01:24.162 --> 00:01:25.980
The head coach of the Calgary Stampeders.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.040
He called me and he said,

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.306
"Hey, I know we cut you

00:01:28.306 --> 00:01:29.418
"but I'd like you to come back."

00:01:29.418 --> 00:01:31.112
I said, "Okay, I appreciate that, coach.

00:01:31.112 --> 00:01:32.158
"Thank you very much.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.201
"I'll think about it."

00:01:33.201 --> 00:01:34.034
He said, "Okay, great."

00:01:34.034 --> 00:01:36.642
I hung up the phone and my dad said,

00:01:36.642 --> 00:01:38.468
"You going to do it, right?"

00:01:38.468 --> 00:01:41.061
I said, "No, I don't think so.

00:01:41.061 --> 00:01:43.469
"I think I'm done with that."

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.685
And he goes, "What?"

00:01:45.685 --> 00:01:48.766
I said, "My gut tells me I'm done."

00:01:48.766 --> 00:01:51.622
He said, "What are you going to do?"

00:01:51.622 --> 00:01:53.277
I took a deep breath,

00:01:53.277 --> 00:01:56.065
I said I'd like to get into the business.

00:01:56.065 --> 00:01:57.174
And he said, "What business?"

00:01:57.174 --> 00:01:59.251
And I said, "The wrestling business."

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:02.802
He says, "You are throwing it all away.

00:02:02.802 --> 00:02:06.076
"It is the worst mistake
you'll ever make."

00:02:06.076 --> 00:02:09.161
He said, "You're ruining your career."

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:11.244
"So maybe I'll be no good

00:02:12.784 --> 00:02:16.617
"but I feel like in my
heart I have to do this

00:02:18.258 --> 00:02:20.091
"and I either need you

00:02:21.838 --> 00:02:22.838
"to train me

00:02:23.962 --> 00:02:25.355
"or need you

00:02:25.355 --> 00:02:27.451
"to not train me."

00:02:27.451 --> 00:02:29.756
My dad rose to the occasion.

00:02:29.756 --> 00:02:31.251
He said, "I'll train."

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.033
And it wound up being

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:35.638
one of the greatest chapters in my life.

00:02:35.638 --> 00:02:38.464
- A lot of people don't
follow their heart.

00:02:38.464 --> 00:02:39.592
Instead what they do is,

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:42.675
they look at a list of
things that could go wrong

00:02:42.675 --> 00:02:44.841
and all the people who would
be disappointed at them

00:02:44.841 --> 00:02:46.479
if it does go wrong.

00:02:46.479 --> 00:02:48.124
And they end up talking themselves

00:02:48.124 --> 00:02:50.154
completely out of this opportunity

00:02:50.154 --> 00:02:51.409
that they have in front of them.

00:02:51.409 --> 00:02:53.796
I precisely remember the moment

00:02:53.796 --> 00:02:56.828
that Evan offered me to work

00:02:56.828 --> 00:03:00.031
and mentor under him full-time

00:03:00.031 --> 00:03:03.085
and he was just saying a lot of details

00:03:03.085 --> 00:03:06.165
and all I could focus on was my heart.

00:03:06.165 --> 00:03:07.415
My heart was saying, "Yes,

00:03:07.415 --> 00:03:09.853
"I'm going to take on this opportunity."

00:03:09.853 --> 00:03:12.132
But I still had to keep my composure

00:03:12.132 --> 00:03:16.139
because I wanted him to go
through the details with me.

00:03:16.139 --> 00:03:19.972
And honestly, that was
the first time in years

00:03:20.929 --> 00:03:23.679
I actually followed my intuition.

00:03:24.619 --> 00:03:27.916
I always pride myself as
someone who is very logical.

00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:30.063
Every opportunity that came my way

00:03:30.063 --> 00:03:31.367
I would make a list

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:34.065
of all the things that's involved.

00:03:34.065 --> 00:03:36.342
I would make a list of all the people

00:03:36.342 --> 00:03:37.931
that's going to be involved

00:03:37.931 --> 00:03:40.544
and all the finances that are involved

00:03:40.544 --> 00:03:44.428
and what I end up doing
is doing nothing at all.

00:03:44.428 --> 00:03:46.721
I just sit and do nothing

00:03:46.721 --> 00:03:48.877
and nothing happened with my life.

00:03:48.877 --> 00:03:53.232
And soon all of that just amount
to a huge amount of regret.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:54.656
Every single day I'm like,

00:03:54.656 --> 00:03:57.119
"I'm going to regret not
taking on this opportunity

00:03:57.119 --> 00:04:00.783
but yet I would just
overthink everything through

00:04:00.783 --> 00:04:02.495
and I started to think about

00:04:02.495 --> 00:04:04.263
when on my deathbed,

00:04:04.263 --> 00:04:06.891
what would I do with all these regrets?

00:04:06.891 --> 00:04:10.498
I didn't want to regret not
taking on opportunities anymore.

00:04:10.498 --> 00:04:12.964
So before I even got a
chance to think about

00:04:12.964 --> 00:04:14.368
the offer he gave me,

00:04:14.368 --> 00:04:17.637
my heart just said yes and
I was going to take it on.

00:04:17.637 --> 00:04:19.537
And I knew it was going to work out

00:04:19.537 --> 00:04:22.146
'cause it felt right deep inside me.

00:04:22.146 --> 00:04:24.957
Even though a lot of people
started questioning me

00:04:24.957 --> 00:04:27.581
and said, "Well, you don't
really have a business plan.

00:04:27.581 --> 00:04:29.423
"You don't even know what the plan is.

00:04:29.423 --> 00:04:31.115
"You don't know if it's going to pan out."

00:04:31.115 --> 00:04:33.734
And I just kind of sat back
and I thought to myself,

00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:36.960
"No, it's going to work
out because I have faith

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.216
"that we're doing the right thing."

00:04:39.216 --> 00:04:43.050
And I'm so glad that I
actually listened to my heart

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:46.286
and not my brain overthinking
things constantly

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.497
because every morning that I'd wake up

00:04:48.497 --> 00:04:51.327
I am so fulfilled with my life

00:04:51.327 --> 00:04:55.138
and I know every day
that I walk in and I work

00:04:55.138 --> 00:04:57.293
I know I'm living out dream

00:04:57.293 --> 00:05:00.114
and I'm not going to regret any of this.

00:05:00.114 --> 00:05:01.164
So I challenge you,

00:05:01.164 --> 00:05:02.890
next time you find yourself

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:05.653
at a crossroads of an opportunity,

00:05:05.653 --> 00:05:08.078
don't overthink anything.

00:05:08.078 --> 00:05:10.453
Just do and follow your heart.

00:05:10.453 --> 00:05:12.342
So the question of the day is

00:05:12.342 --> 00:05:15.693
when was the last time
you followed your heart?

00:05:15.693 --> 00:05:17.750
I would love to read your comments

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.303
and I'll join in on the discussion.

00:05:19.303 --> 00:05:22.385
So I have a special shoutout
for Felipe Palleros.

00:05:22.385 --> 00:05:23.669
Felipe, thank you so much

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:26.738
for picking up a copy of
Evan's book, Your One Word

00:05:26.738 --> 00:05:29.692
and I hope you enjoyed
it as much as I did.

00:05:29.692 --> 00:05:31.462
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:05:31.462 --> 00:05:32.339
I believe in you

00:05:32.339 --> 00:05:35.018
and I hope you continue
to believe in yourself

00:05:35.018 --> 00:05:36.936
and whatever your one word is

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.212
and we'll see you tomorrow morning

00:05:38.212 --> 00:05:41.044
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:41.044 --> 00:05:43.304
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:43.304 --> 00:05:47.003
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:05:47.003 --> 00:05:50.111
(keys clacking)

00:05:50.111 --> 00:05:52.667
- Paul, when you first
signed up for the first one

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:55.621
which was back in '99, 2000?

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:58.413
And did you think you'd
be sitting here in 2013

00:05:58.413 --> 00:05:59.979
talking about number six?

00:05:59.979 --> 00:06:01.904
- No, not a chance.

00:06:01.904 --> 00:06:03.966
No screenplay, nothing when I signed on.

00:06:03.966 --> 00:06:05.737
It was just an idea.
- Yeah.

00:06:05.737 --> 00:06:07.739
- It was funny because I wanted to do it,

00:06:07.739 --> 00:06:09.061
working with my friends

00:06:09.061 --> 00:06:10.659
'cause I'd already worked
with these people before

00:06:10.659 --> 00:06:12.077
and they're like, "You can't do it."

00:06:12.077 --> 00:06:13.175
My representatives were telling me,

00:06:13.175 --> 00:06:14.108
"You can't do it.

00:06:14.108 --> 00:06:15.602
"There's no script,
there's nothing" and then--

00:06:15.602 --> 00:06:17.237
- You didn't listen to their advice.

00:06:17.237 --> 00:06:18.070
- You were right.

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:18.952
- I got lucky.

00:06:18.952 --> 00:06:19.785
But it was just,

00:06:19.785 --> 00:06:20.960
following your heart kind of thing

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.425
and it wasn't even about down the road.

00:06:23.425 --> 00:06:24.750
It was about living in the moment.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:25.591
I got lucky.

00:06:25.591 --> 00:06:27.569
- [Announcer] This young
dedicated artist can't help

00:06:27.569 --> 00:06:30.004
but reflect on those who once doubted him.

00:06:30.004 --> 00:06:32.176
- They never said I
wasn't talented enough.

00:06:32.176 --> 00:06:33.288
They'd say something like,

00:06:33.288 --> 00:06:34.151
"The industry is shady.

00:06:34.151 --> 00:06:35.722
"You'll need to be doing this."

00:06:35.722 --> 00:06:36.938
I respected their opinions

00:06:36.938 --> 00:06:38.966
but at the end of the day
I had to follow my heart

00:06:38.966 --> 00:06:40.872
and that's what I want to do with passion.

00:06:40.872 --> 00:06:42.072
I couldn't shake it

00:06:42.072 --> 00:06:44.499
and I'd be hurt now if
I didn't stick with it

00:06:44.499 --> 00:06:46.835
'cause it'll always be on my head.

00:06:46.835 --> 00:06:49.765
- What is it about investment
and entrepreneurship

00:06:49.765 --> 00:06:52.370
that sort of has bitten you?

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:55.856
- I never look at it as
investments, believe it or not.

00:06:55.856 --> 00:06:58.871
I just look at it as partnerships,

00:06:58.871 --> 00:07:00.521
help changing the world

00:07:00.521 --> 00:07:03.982
and just being part of
something that's inspiring.

00:07:03.982 --> 00:07:05.198
My business people all the time,

00:07:05.198 --> 00:07:06.158
whenever they talk about money,

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:07.592
you can ask them, I go, "Ah!"

00:07:07.592 --> 00:07:11.274
I don't want to hear it but
if they bring an idea to me

00:07:11.274 --> 00:07:13.531
that I think is going
to go to the next level,

00:07:13.531 --> 00:07:14.806
most of the time if I follow

00:07:14.806 --> 00:07:15.639
my heart

00:07:15.639 --> 00:07:17.264
then everything else will fall in place.

00:07:17.264 --> 00:07:18.898
I've never ever done a deal,

00:07:18.898 --> 00:07:20.758
"Ey, we got this suit company.

00:07:20.758 --> 00:07:22.321
"We throw some pinstripes in the suit.

00:07:22.321 --> 00:07:23.648
"You give me a 100,000.

00:07:23.648 --> 00:07:25.231
"We sell 20 of 'em we make."

00:07:25.231 --> 00:07:26.297
I've never done a deal

00:07:26.297 --> 00:07:28.044
where it was always based on money.

00:07:28.044 --> 00:07:29.402
I've always done my business deals

00:07:29.402 --> 00:07:32.083
based on how I felt it was
going to go in the future,

00:07:32.083 --> 00:07:34.689
how I felt it was going to
help and inspire somebody.

